            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
              <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-charcoal-900">What is the difference between cold press and standard models?</h3>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-steel-600">Cold press models (HN426, HN480) operate at higher system pressure (70 Mpa) and cake pressure (42-48 Mpa/cm²), allowing them to extract oil without heating the seeds. This preserves natural nutrients, flavor, and color — resulting in premium-grade oil that commands higher prices. Standard models use lower pressure and may require pre-heating seeds for optimal yield.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-steel-100 p-6 group shadow-sm">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
              <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-charcoal-900">Should I choose single or double barrel?</h3>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-steel-600">If you're just starting out, a single barrel is sufficient and more affordable. For commercial operations, we strongly recommend double barrel — it nearly doubles your throughput while sharing the same hydraulic system, making it much more cost-effective per kg of oil produced. The double barrel allows continuous operation: while one barrel is pressing, you can load the other.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-steel-100 p-6 group shadow-sm">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
              <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-charcoal-900">Can the barrel size be customized?</h3>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-steel-600">Yes! The standard barrel inner diameter is 390mm and height is 800mm, but both can be customized to suit your specific oil seed and production requirements. For example, our sesame model uses a 300mm barrel for higher pressure, and our coconut model uses a 600mm barrel for larger volume. Contact us to discuss your customization needs.</p>
          </details>
